ess I read I wrote at 260 words a  minute by the time I got there the world  speed champion writes at 280 words a  minute so I mean it's a great feel and  she asks you know if you have to slow  them down in nürnberg well I you know  when I do a longer a full presentation I  tell about how the court reporters work  nürnberg we had half shorthand reporters  like I was with a pen and a reporter's  notebook half steno type reporters and  we could never nor in Congress can we  ever interrupt Ted Kennedy anybody else  who's speaking  especially a Ted Kennedy who never aims  a sentence and I reported him over a  period of three years but you just have  to sometimes we had congressmen who  loved to reel off a sentence as did Jim  Wright in Texas in Spanish and then we  wrote sounds and I went to the  congressman later and asked him to  translate for me or spell those Spanish  words in Spanish if that's what he  wanted to see in the congressional  record which nobody else could read but  in the courtroom you can if you get  behind or if you have a witness that is  not intelligible and you can't  understand it but I just don't ever  remember having to stop anybody now in  the Nuremberg the interpreters are the  ones who had the problems because we  reporters had to wait for the  interpreters to translate the the words  and I don't know German but I understand  that in German the verb comes at the end  of the sentence  and so the interpreter had to wait until  the end of the sentence to get the verb  and the current reporter waited for the  interpreter and then he telescope that  sentence as fast as he possibly could  because the next sentence is already  being spoken but at any rate if a  reporter is qualified they can handle it  yes two questions were the were there  other reporters who translate or were  they only transcribed in English for the  Nuremberg trials and when did you decide  to write your book and tell us about  that I'm going to answer your second  question first Toni thank you very much  for it this reporting these trials cost  me so many problems I was so horrified  by it that when as soon as I got back to  this country I started having nightmares  and I was always escaping through a  tunnel for some reason with four or five  small children I was escaping from a  concentration camp and therefore it  might have been Tara seen the children's  camp in a tunnel and I was trying to  keep these children quiet because the  Nazi guard was marching back and forth  along the barbed wire fence with his  bayonetted rifle I didn't want the guard  to hear the children I kept looking for  the light at the end of that tunnel this  went on for three years and it was pure  torture for me and I was so horrified  that I could not speak about it I have  empathy with these survivors and I don't  know whether we have served  fighters in this room but I've spoken to  I think most of them in the Jewish  community here in Denver but I was so  horrified I never talked about it I  never talked about it I was in the  unofficial reporter in the Denver  District Court within eight years after  I got back from Nuremberg and I didn't  talk about it no one talked about it and  I just shoved it all in the back of my  mind and thought nothing about it until  1987 when in Denver we had a high school  teacher in a high school in Aurora who  referred to the Holocaust to her senior  students as the whole of hawks and the  she claimed that she was trying to to  make her students do critical thinking  but at any rate I I was just living and  I decided to get my material and  photographs and in my full presentation  I do a PowerPoint I couldn't do it here  tonight because of time but I have 38  captured German film and I got all of  that out which I had stored in boxes for  40 years and I put together a lecture  which I started giving in 1989 all over  the countries thousands and thousands of  students who were my target audiences  and then in 1995 the Steven Spielberg  Foundation interviewed me here in Denver  and I was beginning to get  confrontations by Holocaust deniers  claiming that it never happened and in  1999 I was speaking at the Long Beach  Hilton hotel to a good-sized audience  the LA Times gave me huge publicity in  advance the day before and  the result the Hilton Hotel received  calls from quote historians asking where  and when in the hotel I would be  speaking and not whether they could  attend the hotel told them it was a  private professional association not  open to the public they demanded that  they be allowed to go in and the hotel  calls me the night before I flew him to  LA and asked me to register under an  assumed name they would put on  additional security  I flew in registered under another name  and I spoke on Saturday afternoon to  this large group my presentation is  about an hour and a half long including  the slides and at the end when people  were asking me questions suddenly the  the doors to the right of me flew open  and an armed security guard with a gun  on his yep came up to me on the podium  and said quietly I have to take you off  the podium right no I knew something was  happening and I went right with him  behind the podium out the door into an  elevator there and down to the basement  for protection so at that time I decided  it's time I write this book and recently  a doctor asked me how I felt doctors  have received the book extremely well  asked me how I felt now that I have the  book finished and I said I have found  the light at the end of that tunnel  [Applause]  they'll exist if so where are they  stored there in archives in Maryland I  say okay my notes of the Nuremberg  trials I said okay they're all in  archives and I want to tell you that the  court reporters transcript of the  doctor's trial is eleven thousand five  hundred thirty eight pages long in  archives and the staff the attorneys and  staff at Nuremberg condemns those eleven  thousand pages down to thirteen